  "statement": "You are given an `n × m` grid of integers and `q` queries. Each query gives `r1 c1 r2 c2` (1-indexed, inclusive corners, `r1 ≤ r2`, `c1 ≤ c2`). Print the sum of the values inside that rectangle.\n\n**Input.** First line `n m q`. Then `n` lines of `m` integers. Then `q` lines, each `r1 c1 r2 c2`.\n\n**Output.** `q` lines, one sum per query.\n\n**Example.**\n\nInput:\n```\n3 3 2\n1 2 3\n4 5 6\n7 8 9\n1 1 3 3\n2 2 3 3\n```\nOutput:\n```\n45\n28\n```",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n, m ≤ 60, 1 ≤ q ≤ 600 in this browser version (the idea scales to 1000 × 1000 grids and 2·10^5 queries)",
    "−1000 ≤ each value ≤ 1000"
  ],
