  "hints": [
    "A 1D prefix sum answers a range. What would a prefix over a 2D grid mean?",
    "Let `P[i][j]` be the sum of the rectangle from `(1,1)` to `(i,j)`. Build it with inclusion-exclusion from `P[i-1][j]`, `P[i][j-1]`, `P[i-1][j-1]`.",
    "Query = `P[r2][c2] - P[r1-1][c2] - P[r2][c1-1] + P[r1-1][c1-1]`: subtract the two strips, add back the corner subtracted twice."
  ],
  "editorial": "Define `P[i][j]` as the sum over rows `1..i` and columns `1..j`, with zero padding on row 0 and column 0. Then `P[i][j] = a[i][j] + P[i-1][j] + P[i][j-1] - P[i-1][j-1]` (the overlap is counted twice, so subtract it once). A query rectangle equals the big prefix `P[r2][c2]`, minus the strip above it (`P[r1-1][c2]`), minus the strip to its left (`P[r2][c1-1]`), plus the corner `P[r1-1][c1-1]` that both removals took away. Build is `O(nm)`, each query `O(1)`.\n\nAt real scale values and sums need 64-bit integers.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n^2)",
    "space": "O(n^2)"
  },
